<title>BAHAMAS: GOVERNMENT LIST.</title>
<headline>GOVERNMENT LIST.</headline>
<text>
<p>BAHAMAS GOVERNMENT LIST (970319)</p>
<p>   **********************************************************</p>
<p>   * 15 Mar 97 - The ruling Free National Movement scored a *</p>
<p>   *		 landslide victory in the Mar 14 general    *</p>
<p>   *		 election, winning 34 of the 40 seats in    *</p>
<p>   *		 parliament.					  *</p>
<p>   **********************************************************</p>
<p>				   - - - - - -</p>
<p>  Governor-General............Orville TURNQUEST</p>
<p>				   - - - - - -</p>
<p>FREE NATIONAL MOVEMENT (FNM) GOVERNMENT:</p>
<p>(Reshuffled 19 Mar 97)</p>
<p>  Prime Minister.............Hubert A. INGRAHAM</p>
<p>(Sworn in for second term 18 Mar 97)</p>
<p>  Deputy Prime Minister.........Frank A. WATSON</p>
<p>(Also Minister for National Security)</p>
<p>				   - - - - - -</p>
<p>MINISTERS (only names confirmed so far after reshuffle):</p>
<p>  Attorney General &amp; Justice Minister...........Tennyson WELLS</p>
<p>  Education........Ivy L. DUMONT</p>
<p>  Foreign Affairs.............Janet G. BOSTWICK</p>
<p>  Housing &amp; Social Development...Algernon ALLEN</p>
<p>  Labour, Immigration &amp; Training........Theresa MOXEY-INGRAHAM</p>
<p>  National Security...............See Deputy PM</p>
<p>  Tourism.............C.A. SMITH</p>
<p>				   - - - - - -</p>
<p>  Central Bank Governor..........James H. SMITH</p>
<p>				   - - - - - -</p>
<p>	 NOTE: Any comments/queries on the content of this</p>
<p>		 government list, please contact the Reuter</p>
<p>		 Editorial Reference Unit, London, on (171) 542</p>
<p>		 7968.</p>
<p>				 (End Government List)</p>
